## 1. System Overview

The Agento v2.1 system is **three simple tools for a solopreneur**, none of them
agentic:

1. **Storefront** — Next.js App Router editorial site (home, `/tienda`, `/blog`).
   Hydrates from Payload headless via server components. Spanish, COP. No cart,
   no checkout: CTAs route to WhatsApp (`wa.me`) so the buyer contacts Shirley
   directly. (BRD §3.1 Cap 01, PRD §3.1)
2. **Intrinsic CRM** — Payload admin (`/admin`) with two operator-facing
   collections, `products` (Catalog) and `orders` (Dispatches), plus the
   `posts` collection backing the blog. Shirley creates products, confirms
   payments (`CHECKOUT_READY → PAID`), marks dispatches
   (`PAID → DISPATCHED`), cancels orders (admin only).
   (BRD §3.1 Cap 02–03, PRD §3.2–3.3)
3. **Telegram Command Center** — a single Telegram bot that is **Shirley's**
   mobile command nexus (not a customer-facing chatbot): real-time pings on new
   orders, `/pagado`, `/despachado`, `/pedido`, `/pendientes`, `/help`, `/nuevo`
   for manual order registration, photo-to-draft for catalog capture, and a 09:00
   America/Bogota daily digest. (BRD §3.1 Cap 04, PRD §3.4)

### What is deliberately NOT in the runtime path (v2.1)

There is **no LLM in the runtime path**. The following v1.0 components are
**explicitly removed** and must not reappear in code, env, or comments:

- ~~Vercel AI SDK~~ — frozen for the agentic phase.
- ~~Gemini 2.5 Flash~~ — frozen for the agentic phase.
- ~~Gemini Embedding 2~~ / ~~pgvector~~ — no semantic search in v2.1.
- ~~Pre-LLM Guardian~~ — no LLM to protect.
- ~~n8n orchestration~~ — async work lives in Next.js route handlers + external
  cron. (PRD §4 — Maintainability: "no external orchestration tools".)
- ~~Payment gateway (Wompi/Stripe)~~ — settlement is external (Nequi, transfer,
  cash on delivery). Shirley confirms manually via Telegram or admin.
  (BRD §3.2, PRD §2 `**No LLM in MVP**`.)
- ~~`token_usage_logs`~~ / ~~Unit Economics cost metric~~ — no tokens to audit
  in v2.1. (BRD §6 note, PRD changelog v1.1 → v2.0.)

### Topology

The system is a pnpm monorepo (BRD §3.1 Cap 05): `apps/web` (storefront +
Payload admin embedded + Telegram webhook route), `packages/db` (Drizzle),
`packages/types` (payload-types + Zod), `packages/telegram` (command handler).
Single deploy, end-to-end TypeScript. `tsc --noEmit` blocks merge.

