## 3. Module Breakdown

| Module | Responsibility | Technology |
|---|---|---|
| Storefront | Editorial home + masonry gallery (`/tienda`) + blog (`/blog`, `/blog/[slug]`). WhatsApp-only CTA, no cart. Hydrates from Payload via server components. ISR + on-demand revalidation on `afterChange`. | Next.js App Router (Turbopack) |
| Payload Admin (CRM) | Authenticated admin with Catalog (`products`), Dispatches (`orders`), and `posts` collections. Status transitions: `CHECKOUT_READY → PAID → DISPATCHED`, `CANCELLED` (admin only). | Payload CMS (embedded in `apps/web`) |
| Drizzle DB layer | Type-safe DB access, schema mirroring Payload collections. Types shared via `packages/types` to keep Drizzle and `payload-types.ts` in sync. | Drizzle ORM (`packages/db`) |
| Telegram Webhook Route | Single Next.js route handler receiving Telegram updates; validates `X-Telegram-Bot-Api-Secret-Token` and authorized chat ID before any DB access. | Next.js Route Handler (`apps/web`) |
| Telegram Command Handler | Parses commands (`/nuevo`, `/pagado`, `/despachado`, `/pedido`, `/pendientes`, `/help`), photo uploads, unrecognized text. Mutates Payload, replies via Telegram Bot API. Idempotent `/pagado` and `/despachado`. | `packages/telegram` |
| Daily Digest Cron | 09:00 America/Bogota scheduled POST that queries Payload for yesterday's activity and pushes a digest to Shirley. | External cron (e.g. Upstash QStash) → Next.js Route Handler |
| Photo Storage | Stores photo-to-draft uploads from Telegram `getFile`. `/public/` is read-only on Vercel, so production media lives here. | Supabase Storage (bucket `product-drafts`) |

There is intentionally no "Closing Agent", no "Web Agent Orchestrator", no
"Embedding Engine", no "Pre-LLM Guardian", and no "Async Orchestration via n8n".
Those modules were part of the frozen v1.0 agentic design and are out of scope
for v2.1. (BRD §3.2 — Explicitly out of scope.)

