## 4. Database Design

Engine: PostgreSQL (Supabase) accessed by Payload and by Drizzle in
`packages/db`. **No pgvector extension, no embeddings, no vector index, no
`token_usage_logs`.** Only three operator-facing collections back the MVP, plus
the Payload-internal `users` collection:

| Collection | Purpose | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `products` | Single source of truth for the catalog. Edited only from Payload admin or photo-to-draft (which creates a draft with `available = false`). | Fields: `name`, `description`, `price_cop`, `materials[]`, `images[{url}]`, `available` (default true), `handoff_ttl_hours` (DEPRECATED, unused in v2.1), `is_upsell` (default false, unused in v2.1). Products with `available = false` are **excluded from all public storefront listings**. (PRD §3.1, AC-01.5.) |
| `orders` | Dispatch queue. Status mutates ONLY via admin buttons or Telegram commands. | Fields: `sessionCode` (unique, format `AX-XXXX`), `customerName`, `customerPhone`, `customerAddress`, `items[{productId, name, price_cop, quantity}]`, `totalPrice`, `status` (`CHECKOUT_READY \| PAID \| DISPATCHED \| CANCELLED`), `paymentMethod` (`Nequi \| Transferencia \| Efectivo`), `paidAt`, `dispatchedAt`. `items` stores an **immutable price snapshot** — later product price changes do not affect existing orders. (PRD §3.3, AC-03.5.) |
| `posts` | Blog content backing `/blog` and `/blog/[slug]`. | Fields: `title`, `excerpt`, `content` (Lexical), `coverImage` (upload → Supabase Storage), `author`, `category`, `format` (`standard \| quote \| audio`), `audioUrl`, `quoteText`, `quoteAuthor`, `publishedAt`, `slug`. (PRD §3.2.) |
| `users` (internal) | Admin auth. | `auth: true`. Admin login only. (PRD §3.3.) |

Shirley's authorized Telegram chat ID and the webhook secret live in
environment variables, not in the database. All types are generated by
Payload (`payload-types.ts`) and re-exported by `packages/types` so Drizzle
and the Telegram handler share the same shape; a drift check (build script)
fails the build on mismatch.

### Removed tables (relative to v1.0)

| Removed | Reason |
|---|---|
| `product_embeddings` | No pgvector / no semantic search in v2.1. (BRD §3.2.) |
| `token_usage_logs` | No LLM in runtime — no tokens to audit. (BRD §6 note.) |
| `sessions` (frozen intent) | No Intent Chips / no WhatsApp handoff in v2.1. |
| `dispatch_sheets` | No auto-generated dispatch sheet; Shirley packs manually. |

